  :tutorial/content "**MTH 255 — Recitation Worksheet 5**\n\nDue: 2026-10-29\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline source: [Canvas — Week 5 Recitation Session](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064132/assignments/10705975), checked 2026-10-26; Canvas lists Thursday at 11:59 p.m.\nDate imported: 2026-10-26\nSource: [255-R5.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2F255-R5.pdf)\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and explicitly labeled reference sketches are independently authored additions. Source figures and problem statements are retained; domain and theorem-hypothesis qualifications are explained in the reveal fields.\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Complete all five problems and every labeled subpart. Show supporting work, including the requested sketches, proofs, and methods.\n- The PDF states that recitation worksheets are graded for completeness. Canvas describes attendance and participation grading and states that late work is not accepted.\n- Work on the printed template, write/type on the PDF with a tablet, or use your own paper with the same layout.\n- Upload one PDF to Gradescope under **Recitation Worksheet 5**. Preserve the six-page template format: a cover page followed by one page per problem, including any blank problems. If a problem uses multiple physical pages, combine them into one collage page for that problem. An incorrectly formatted PDF receives zero under the source instructions.\n- For regions with holes, use the entire positively oriented boundary: outer boundaries counterclockwise and inner boundaries clockwise. For flux, outward means outward from the shaded region, including into its holes."
