 {:db/id "e5c996e0-6d97-56e4-b860-1a7299c3faf3"
  :question/id #uuid "e5c996e0-6d97-56e4-b860-1a7299c3faf3"
  :question/problem "**(c)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{y}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1c.png)"
  :question/answer-fields ["797ab717-31ad-5200-80d3-40e0eff47f89"]
  :question/worked-solution "The field is undefined at the origin. Locally, $\\theta_x=-y/r^2$ and $\\theta_y=x/r^2$, so $\\psi_y=F_1$ and $-\\psi_x=F_2$. If a global stream function existed, its gradient would be $(-y/r^2,x/r^2)$, whose circulation around the unit circle is $2\\pi$, impossible for a gradient. Circle and ray families still describe equipotentials and streamlines geometrically."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
 {:db/id "8649c722-5aa8-51db-997f-16dc40aaf4af"
  :answer/id #uuid "8649c722-5aa8-51db-997f-16dc40aaf4af"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "A potential is locally $\\phi=\\theta=\\arg(x+iy)$ on a chosen angle branch; there is no single-valued global potential on the full punctured plane. A global stream function is $\\psi=-\\tfrac12\\ln(x^2+y^2)=-\\ln r$.\n\nLocal equipotentials are radial rays $\\theta=c$, and streamlines are circles $r=e^{-k}$ traversed counterclockwise. Draw a couple of rays and a couple of circles, excluding the origin.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part d](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1d.png)"
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
