 {:db/id "396b73fa-e153-52a7-b857-cef12407f39e"
  :question/id #uuid "396b73fa-e153-52a7-b857-cef12407f39e"
  :question/problem "**(d)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1d.png)"
  :question/answer-fields ["8eee3749-21bf-5848-8c47-26f83fcbc9d4"]
  :question/worked-solution "Check $\\psi_y=-y/r^2=F_1$ and $-\\psi_x=x/r^2=F_2$. The field's unit-circle circulation is $2\\pi$, ruling out a global potential. A continuous angle branch works on a cut domain, for example $\\theta=\\arctan(y/x)$ on $x>0$. Additive constants in any valid potential or stream function do not change the field."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
