 {:db/id "0090f78f-b0b8-5835-9b37-323e92c257c8"
  :question/id #uuid "0090f78f-b0b8-5835-9b37-323e92c257c8"
  :question/problem "**(a)** Find the counterclockwise circulation of $\\mathbf F=\\langle-2y,3x\\rangle$ around the boundary of the shaded region. Include every boundary component or segment, with the region on the left.\n\n![Annular sector between radii 1 and 2, excluding the right-hand sector between y=-x and y=x](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannular-sector-2a.png)\n\nCirculation: {{answer}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["351d661a-c568-5d01-89d7-7d83c416279b"]
  :question/worked-solution "The pictured region is $1\\le r\\le2$, $\\pi/4\\le\\theta\\le7\\pi/4$. Its angular width is $3\\pi/2$, so its area is $\\tfrac12(2^2-1^2)(3\\pi/2)=9\\pi/4$. The scalar curl is $\\partial_x(3x)-\\partial_y(-2y)=3+2=5$. Green's theorem gives circulation $5(9\\pi/4)=45\\pi/4$. The boundary includes the outer arc, two radial segments, and the inner arc in its opposite orientation."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
