 {:db/id "6723d5bd-2fd9-5cdf-9e93-3864827f6161"
  :question/id #uuid "6723d5bd-2fd9-5cdf-9e93-3864827f6161"
  :question/problem "**(b)** Find the counterclockwise circulation of $\\mathbf F=\\langle0,xy\\rangle$ around the boundary of the shaded region.\n\n![Upper half-annulus between radii 1 and 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fupper-half-annulus-2b.png)\n\nCirculation: {{answer}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["cd6a9e3a-5016-57c4-8f06-962ad56b5407"]
  :question/worked-solution "Here $1\\le r\\le2$, $0\\le\\theta\\le\\pi$, and $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\partial_x(xy)=y$. Hence\n\n$$\\oint_{\\partial R}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\iint_R y\\,dA=\\int_0^\\pi\\int_1^2 r^2\\sin\\theta\\,dr\\,d\\theta=\\frac73\\cdot2=\\frac{14}{3}.$$\n\nThe entire boundary is used, including the inner semicircle. The field is smooth on a neighborhood of the region."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
