 {:db/id "de548bef-88d0-5a3d-b4d8-48dc735f22f5"
  :question/id #uuid "de548bef-88d0-5a3d-b4d8-48dc735f22f5"
  :question/problem "**(a)** Find the flux of $\\mathbf F=\\nabla(x^2+y^2)$ out of the shaded region.\n\n![Annulus with inner radius 1 and outer radius 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannulus-3a.png)\n\nOutward flux: {{answer}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["04f73045-cd53-5ed1-a512-8b548add7cd5"]
  :question/worked-solution "The field is $\\mathbf F=(2x,2y)$, with divergence $2+2=4$. The annulus has area $\\pi(2^2-1^2)=3\\pi$, so the flux form of Green's theorem gives $4(3\\pi)=12\\pi$. Independently, the outer-circle flux is $4\\cdot4\\pi=16\\pi$, and the inner-circle flux is $(-2)\\cdot2\\pi=-4\\pi$, since outward from the annulus points toward the hole there. Their sum is $12\\pi$."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
