 {:db/id "1f62ce36-36d9-5278-8736-218e35f12b54"
  :question/id #uuid "1f62ce36-36d9-5278-8736-218e35f12b54"
  :question/problem "**(b)** Find the flux of $\\mathbf F=\\nabla\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$ out of the shaded region.\n\n![Annulus with inner radius 1 and outer radius 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannulus-3b.png)\n\nOutward flux: {{answer}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["0a634087-b4ac-5ca2-8e59-3cd0853c52df"]
  :question/worked-solution "For $r>0$, $\\mathbf F=(x/r,y/r)$ and $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=1/r$. The origin is outside the annulus, so Green's theorem applies on this region:\n\n$$\\iint_R\\frac1r\\,dA=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_1^2\\frac1r\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta=2\\pi.$$\n\nDirectly, the outer flux is $4\\pi$ and the inner flux is $-2\\pi$, giving $2\\pi$. Omitting the inner boundary would give the wrong answer."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
