 {:db/id "7caf2745-ec66-5f08-acba-1fbed834af52"
  :question/id #uuid "7caf2745-ec66-5f08-acba-1fbed834af52"
  :question/problem "**(b)** Show that on the top and bottom edges of $R$, the line integral $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds$ is zero."
  :question/answer-fields ["f3eb20ba-2856-5c6d-bb39-77a2afde1460"]
  :question/worked-solution "The field is vertical, whereas the tangent to either horizontal edge is horizontal. Their dot product vanishes regardless of which horizontal edge is traversed left-to-right."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
 {:db/id "6b8da09c-3144-58f9-a42b-54e2421ef65f"
  :answer/id #uuid "6b8da09c-3144-58f9-a42b-54e2421ef65f"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "The counterclockwise orientation traverses the right edge upward from $(b,0)$ to $(b,1)$. Parametrize it by $\\mathbf r(t)=(b,t)$, $0\\le t\\le1$. Then\n\n$$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\int_0^1(0,f(b))\\cdot(0,1)\\,dt=f(b).$$"
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
