 {:db/id "c4866e18-4bc1-5a67-be39-b6bc4d1e9f3a"
  :question/id #uuid "c4866e18-4bc1-5a67-be39-b6bc4d1e9f3a"
  :question/problem "**(e)** Apply the circulation form of Green's theorem to $\\mathbf F$ on $R$. What theorem do you get?"
  :question/answer-fields ["f9da95b7-b36d-5ce9-b0d8-8239c9ee51a7"]
  :question/worked-solution "Sum the four oriented edges first: $0+f(b)+0-f(a)$. The rectangle's height is one, so the double integral reduces directly to the one-variable integral. Do not claim the standard Green argument is justified by mere differentiability without addressing this hypothesis gap."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
